# Jira GRW-181 — the ignore file for `docker build -f web/Dockerfile .`
#
# BuildKit looks for `<dockerfile-path>.dockerignore` before falling back to
# the context root's `.dockerignore`. That fallback would be wrong here: the
# root file ends with
#
#     web/*
#     !web/package.json
#
# because the api/worker image deliberately carries no dashboard. Building the
# dashboard against that ignore file yields a context with no dashboard in it —
# and the failure is a confusing "module not found" deep in `next build`, not a
# missing-file error.
#
# So this file exists to say the opposite: keep web/, drop the API's world.

node_modules
web/node_modules
.git
.github
.cognito
coverage
uploads
dist
*.log
*.tsbuildinfo

# Never in an image.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# The API's own source and tests are not part of the dashboard build. Its
# package.json stays — npm workspaces needs it to resolve the workspace at all.
src
test
docs
scripts
Dockerfile
docker-compose*.yml

# Next rebuilds these; a stale local copy would be baked in.
web/.next

# The dashboard's own unit tests. `next build` type-checks everything it can
# see, and these import the API's source across the workspace boundary
# (`../../../../src/api/security/tenant-policy`) — which is excluded above and
# should stay excluded. They are tests; `npm test` runs them, a production
# image has no business carrying them, and their absence is what lets the
# build's typecheck pass without dragging src/ into the context.
web/**/*.test.ts
web/**/*.test.tsx
